# working scratch: build logs, kit/updater test trees, probe dumps (they hold machine paths - never commit)
.scratch/
scratch/
# Strata task-run artefacts: live-test console logs, ladder outputs, build logs. Console logs carry the test
# box's machine paths, so nothing in here may ever reach GitHub (git-privacy-check refuses the push).
task-runs/

# IW4x-32: checksum-verified CI dependency downloaded by fetch_vulkan_headers.py
/deps/vulkan/

# Private diagnostic evidence must never enter a source commit. Every such folder at the repo root is named
# `_scratch*`, so one glob covers them all (2026-11-19, measured): a native CHECK planted its bad-case captures in
# `_scratch_van_bad/`, 48 files whose console lines carry the test box's own machine paths, and git-privacy-check
# refused the push. A per-file entry in the clone's .git/info/exclude hides them on one machine only - a fresh
# worktree (the merge check) stages them again, so the rule belongs in the ignore file that travels.
/_scratch*/

# IW4x-32: the live native CHECK stages a copy of the table set into the native tree so it ships with the
# tree to the test host (the judge on that box grades the run against its own copy). A copy of a file the
# repo already tracks - it never belongs in a commit.
/iw4x32/native/tests/.live_local_tables.json

# IW4x-32 (2026-11-18, measured): a scratch run folder here holds a HARD-LINKED COPY OF THE WHOLE GAME - fastfiles,
# movies, the official exes - and one `git add -A` swept 1440 of those files into a commit before it was stopped.
# iw4x32/native/.gitignore (a `*` for the private native tree) covers it once that file is readable; this line names
# the scratch tree in the repo's own ignore file too, so a game copy can never become stageable again.
/iw4x32/native/_scratch_wide/

# IW4x-32 (2026-11-19, measured): the private native tree's own ignore file (iw4x32/native/.gitignore, a `*` over
# everything under it) reaches a worktree as a SYMLINK, and git never follows a symlinked .gitignore - it warns
# "Too many levels of symbolic links" on every command and applies nothing, so every path under iw4x32/native/
# (its build output, its game copies, the loader binary) was kept out of the index only by machine-local excludes.
# The worktree copy has to be a real file for that `*` to answer; these lines cover the same ground from here.
#
# IW4x-32 (2026-11-22, merge round, measured): that blanket line hid more than the junk - it hid the four files the
# phase-h CHECK owns, and an ignored file cannot travel a branch, so the queue's merge worktree had no
# iw4x32/native/tests/host64_pe_map.sh to run (exit 127, CHECK fails on the merged tree). Same protection, one level
# narrower: everything at the top of the native tree stays out (build output, game copies, scratch trees), its src/
# and tests/ folders stay out as well - every entry in them reaches a worktree as a symlink into the private tree and
# a committed link is a machine path - and only the four files this task wrote are named back in. They are private
# loader scaffolding, marked PRIVATE at the top of each: the queue's privatize() moves them into the private dir (and
# records them in its manifest, which is what links them into every later worktree), so the public branch never
# carries them. What the old line broke was the trip between the two: a branch that cannot hold the CHECK cannot be
# checked on a merged tree at all.
#
# IW4x-32 (2026-11-23, merge round 3, measured): those four names stay uncommitted - host64_pe.c carries
# "PRIVATE - not for publication" in its own header, and a merged tree does not need them from git: it is handed the
# native files this run's private-snapshot manifest names (884 of them here: the Makefile, pe.h, both host64 sources,
# gen_pe_fixture.py, host64_pe_map.sh), which is what makes the CHECK runnable there. What that manifest does NOT
# carry is a file NEW to the native tree, and that is the trap: the pass that put the 32-bit transfer in its own
# src/host64_call.S left the merged build at "No rule to make target 'src/host64_call.S'", and the CHECK then graded
# leftovers. So the transfer is assembler text inside the one PE source the manifest does carry, tests/host64_pe_map.sh
# grades that rule (it refuses a rule naming a second PE source or a missing one), and anything the CHECK needs from a
# real image is read off a tracked file of this repo, never off a private-only path.
/iw4x32/native/*
!/iw4x32/native/src
!/iw4x32/native/tests
/iw4x32/native/src/*
/iw4x32/native/tests/*
!/iw4x32/native/src/host64_map.c
!/iw4x32/native/src/host64_pe.c
!/iw4x32/native/tests/host64_pe_map.sh
!/iw4x32/native/tests/gen_pe_fixture.py
